# Input
```html
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<button disabled>Save</button>
<button disabled="false">Save</button>
<input type="submit" disabled>
<div role="button" disabled>Save</div>
<button disabled aria-disabled="true">Save</button>

<input disabled>
<input type="text" disabled="disabled" name="email">
<textarea disabled></textarea>
<input type="text" disabled readonly>

<select disabled></select>
<input type="checkbox" disabled>
<select disabled aria-disabled="true"></select>

<fieldset disabled></fieldset>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalidFix.html:2:9 lint/nursery/noDisabledAttribute  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! Avoid the native disabled attribute on this button.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
  > 2 │ <button disabled>Save</button>
      │         ^^^^^^^^
    3 │ <button disabled="false">Save</button>
    4 │ <input type="submit" disabled>
  
  i A disabled form control can't receive keyboard focus, so it can't be reached with the Tab key.
  
  i Replace it with aria-disabled, which only exposes the disabled state to assistive technology. It does not suppress pointer or keyboard activation, form submission or validation, or apply disabled styling. Implement those behaviors, including forced-colors styling.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use aria-disabled instead.
  
    2 │ <button·aria-disabled="true">Save</button>
      │         +++++        +++++++              

```

